course: dictionary
lesson: 1822
title: Co: a short form and a starter
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Co is a short piece of a word, so you will see it in different places. On a shop sign, «Smith & Co.» is short for company. At the start of a word, co- often means together, as in co-pilot.
explain: Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits. Can you hear a business, a place in Ireland, a letter, or a team? The context tells you. «Co. Kerry» is a county, not a company, because Kerry is a place.
explain: Some words start with co but do not use it as a prefix. «Ancient», «conscience» and «conscious» spell a /sh/ sound with ci or sci. In conscience, the co is just part of the word, so it does not mean together.
fact: Co. is short for company, often in business names such as «& Co.».
fact: In Ireland, Co. is short for county, as in «Co. Dublin».
fact: The prefix co- at the start of a word often means together or jointly, as in co-author and co-worker.
fact: c/o on a letter means «care of», or «at the address of».
fact: CO is the chemical symbol for carbon monoxide, a poisonous gas with no smell, so homes have CO alarms.
exercise: «Smith & Co. sells bread and cakes.» What does Co. stand for? | *company | carbon | cope | county
exercise: A pilot flies the plane and a co-pilot helps fly it with them. What does co- mean in co-pilot? | a loud engine noise | *together, sharing the job | very quickly | underground
exercise: «Co. Kerry» is a place in Ireland. What does Co. mean here? | county | *county, the same as a county | company | copy
test: CO is the chemical symbol for carbon monoxide. Why do many homes have CO alarms? | *to warn you about a dangerous gas that has no smell | to play music at night | to tell the time | to keep the house warm
test: On a letter, «c/o» is written before a name. What does c/o mean? | *at the address of | carried over | company owned | copy of
exam: Which word uses the prefix co- to mean together? | coat | *cooperate | cool | cold
